+## Runner tests pinning the new encoding contract (`internal/store/migrations_test.go`)
+
+- `TestChecksumRecordingIsAnchorHexPlusTaggedBase64`: anchor row is 64-char lowercase-hex
+  TEXT matching the file's independent sha256; the `0002_lights` row is `raw-b64:` TEXT
+  whose payload is exactly 43 chars, decodes as unpadded base64url, and equals the file's
+  digest (tag spelled as a literal in the test, not the production constant); **both rows
+  report `typeof(sha256) = 'text'`** (column-type honesty); both are byte-stable across
+  close+reopen.
+- `TestTamperedSecondMigrationChecksumRefusesOpenNamingItsFile` (table): a later row in
+  the foreign bare-hex encoding is refused **even when the digest is correct**
+  (representations are positional, never negotiated — now proven against a real stale DB,
+  see below), and a wrong digest under the right tag is refused; both name
+  `0002_lights.sql`, not `0001_init.sql`, say "checksum mismatch", and carry the stored
+  value and the file checksum.
+- `TestDBFileHexTokenIsExactlyTheFirstMigrationChecksum`: after Open+ProbeInc+Close the
+  raw DB file contains exactly ONE 64-char lowercase-hex token and it equals the anchor's
+  recorded checksum — holds for any future migration count; a regression (any code writing
+  another hex TEXT token) fails here, in-owned, instead of only in the unowned canary.
+- `TestMigrationChecksumGuard`, `TestRecordedVersionWithoutEmbeddedFileRefusesOpen`,
+  `TestApplyMigrationsAppliesUnrecordedFilesInOrder` (incl. `checkSyntheticFileChecksums`,
+  now comparing per-position expected representations computed from the synthetic file
+  bytes) — unchanged semantics, verified green.
+
+## Public API surface (unchanged since `93762ff`; later tasks compile against this)
+
+```go
+// ids & kind (internal/store/lights.go)
+type LightID int64
+type PhotoID int64
+type Kind string
+const ( KindPark = "park"; KindBuilding = "building"; KindStreet = "street" )
+func ParseKind(s string) (Kind, error)            // exact lowercase match only
+
+// sentinels (errors.Is)
+var ErrDuplicateAssetNo // lights.go — CreateLight/EditLight hitting lights_asset_no
+var ErrNotFound         // store.go — sql.ErrNoRows / no row updated/deleted
+
+// lights (internal/store/lights.go)
+type NewLight struct {
+    AssetNo *string; Kind Kind; Label string; Lat, Lon float64
+    AccuracyM *float64; PhotoID *PhotoID; GmlPoleNo *string; CreatedBy *int64
+}
+type Light struct {
+    ID LightID; AssetNo *string; Kind Kind; Label string; Lat, Lon float64
+    AccuracyM *float64; PhotoID *PhotoID; Status, StatusSource string
+    StatusAt, StatusConfirmedAt *time.Time; GmlPoleNo *string; CreatedBy *int64
+    CreatedAt, UpdatedAt time.Time; DeletedAt *time.Time
+}
+func (db *DB) CreateLight(ctx context.Context, n NewLight) (Light, error) // stamps created_at=updated_at=now (UTC RFC3339); invalid kind → errInvalidKind; dup → ErrDuplicateAssetNo
+func (db *DB) GetLight(ctx context.Context, id LightID) (Light, error)            // deleted/missing → ErrNotFound
+func (db *DB) LightByAssetNo(ctx context.Context, assetNo string) (Light, error)  // live rows only
+func (db *DB) RecentLights(ctx context.Context, limit, offset int) ([]Light, error) // newest-first, id DESC tie-break; negatives refused
+func (db *DB) EditLight(ctx context.Context, id LightID, label string, assetNo *string) (Light, error) // stamps updated_at; missing/deleted → ErrNotFound; dup → ErrDuplicateAssetNo
+func (db *DB) SoftDeleteLight(ctx context.Context, id LightID) error            // stamps deleted_at=now; missing/already-deleted → ErrNotFound; asset_no freed
+func (db *DB) NearbyLights(ctx context.Context, lat, lon, radiusM float64) ([]Light, error) // bbox SUPERSET of the exact disk (safety 1.10); exact Haversine filter is internal/geo's (T-204); negative radius refused
+
+// photos (internal/store/photos.go)
+type NewPhoto struct { Path string; Width, Height int; Bytes int64; SHA256 string }
+type Photo struct { ID PhotoID; OwnerID *int64; Path string; Width, Height int; Bytes int64; SHA256 string; CreatedAt time.Time }
+func (db *DB) CreatePhoto(ctx context.Context, n NewPhoto) (Photo, error) // stamps created_at; UNIQUE path
+func (db *DB) PhotoByID(ctx context.Context, id PhotoID) (Photo, error)   // missing → ErrNotFound
+func (db *DB) PhotoList(ctx context.Context, limit int) ([]Photo, error)  // id order
+
+// runner (internal/store/migrations.go) — encoding contract, this round
+//   schema_migrations(version TEXT PK, sha256 TEXT NOT NULL, applied_at TEXT):
+//   anchor row (first embedded migration) → 64-char lowercase hex;
+//   every later row → "raw-b64:" + unpadded base64url(raw digest);
+//   verification compares the recorded bytes against sumRecordValue(i, m)
+//   (no parsing); all mismatches and ghost versions refuse the boot naming
+//   the offending file (ErrChecksumMismatch). Unexported helpers are pinned
+//   by the tests listed above.
+```
